---------------------------------------------------------------------------
                          DERIVED WORK NOTICE
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

hyprwake is a derivative of hyprflow and carries its git history. It also
ports functionality from hypr-session-restore and its Omarchy fork. All three
are MIT-licensed; their copyright notices are reproduced below and apply to
the portions of this Software derived from them.

  hyprflow — https://github.com/isorensen/hyprflow
  Copyright (c) 2026 iSorensen
    Origin of: the crate layout, trait-based hyprctl/process abstractions,
    named sessions, dry-run, max-age, autosave rotation and systemd timer.

  hypr-session-restore — https://github.com/UpayanChatterjee/hypr-session-restore
  Copyright (c) 2026 Upayan Chatterjee
    Origin of: /proc-derived relaunch commands, terminal cwd and TUI
    detection, exec-rule spawning with silent workspace placement, the
    post-spawn sweep pass for forking apps, pinned/special-workspace
    handling.

  hypr-session-restore (Omarchy fork) — https://github.com/SotoAugusto/hypr-session-restore
  Copyright (c) 2026 SotoAugusto
    Origin of: uwsm-app launching, the empty-save guard, magic-workspace
    selector matching, dispatch-payload error checking, state-dir logging,
    and the Omarchy post-boot / post-update hook wiring.

Each of the above is distributed under the MIT License, whose terms are
reproduced in full at the top of this file.
